@startuml
title Normal Chat Message - Keyboard to Broadcast
autonumber
actor "User A" as UserA
participant "ClientApplication A\nJavaFX view" as ViewA
participant "ClientController A" as ControllerA
participant "ChatClient A" as ClientA
participant "ClientHandler A\nvirtual thread" as HandlerA
participant "ChatServer" as Server
participant "ClientHandler B" as HandlerB
participant "ChatClient B\nreceiving virtual thread" as ClientB
participant "ClientController B" as ControllerB
participant "ClientApplication B\nJavaFX view" as ViewB
actor "User B" as UserB

note over ClientA,ClientB
  Both clients are connected with named USERNAME: handshakes completed.
  Handlers are registered; receiving loops and message listeners are active.
  This diagram covers a normal, nonempty message only.
end note

UserA -> ViewA : Type message; press SEND or ENTER
ViewA -> ControllerA : sendMessage()
ControllerA -> ViewA : Read messageField.getText()
ControllerA -> ControllerA : send(message, false)
note right of ControllerA
  Guards online/readOnly/busy/closed state.
  Starts a virtual thread for the send operation.
end note
ControllerA -> ClientA : sendMessage(message)
ClientA -> ClientA : output.println(message); checkError()
ClientA ->> HandlerA : UTF-8 line over TCP
HandlerA -> HandlerA : input.readLine() returns message
HandlerA -> HandlerA : Format using LocalTime.now() and username
note right of HandlerA
  formatted = [HH:mm] username: message
  Formatting occurs in ClientHandler on the server.
end note
HandlerA -> Server : broadcast(formatted)

loop Each registered handler (A and B shown; order unspecified)
  alt Recipient is A (sender also receives broadcast)
    Server -> HandlerA : sendMessage(formatted)
    HandlerA -> HandlerA : output.println(formatted); checkError()
    HandlerA ->> ClientA : UTF-8 line over TCP
    ClientA -> ControllerA : messageListener.accept(formatted)
    ControllerA ->> ViewA : Platform.runLater(lambda): appendText(formatted + newline)
    ViewA ->> UserA : Display message on JavaFX Application Thread
  else Recipient is B
    Server -> HandlerB : sendMessage(formatted)
    note right of HandlerB
      This sendMessage call executes on A's handler thread.
      B's own handler thread independently reads B's input.
    end note
    HandlerB -> HandlerB : output.println(formatted); checkError()
    HandlerB ->> ClientB : UTF-8 line over TCP
    ClientB -> ClientB : reader.readLine() returns formatted line
    ClientB -> ControllerB : messageListener.accept(formatted)
    ControllerB ->> ViewB : Platform.runLater(lambda): appendText(formatted + newline)
    ViewB ->> UserB : Display message on JavaFX Application Thread
  end
end

note over ControllerA,ClientA
  After a successful send, Controller A also queues
  input clearing and control updates with Platform.runLater().
  These UI updates may interleave with incoming broadcasts.
end note
@enduml
